// roboscope host Pi: what unattended-upgrades may install.
// Deployed from the roboscope repo (hardware/host_pi/rootfs); edit it there, not on the Pi.
//
// 64-bit Pi OS pulls from origin=Debian (deb.debian.org, covered by the stock
// 50unattended-upgrades, including Debian-Security) and origin="Raspberry Pi Foundation"
// (archive.raspberrypi.com: kernel, firmware, Pi tools), which the stock config doesn't
// match. This adds the latter. Checked with `apt-cache policy` on 2026-11-26. This file is
// read after 50-, and list entries are appended to the stock ones.
//
// No automatic reboot: a reboot mid-observation would drop the mount and camera. Check
// for /var/run/reboot-required and reboot by hand between sessions.
Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern {
        "origin=Raspberry Pi Foundation,codename=${distro_codename},label=Raspberry Pi Foundation";
};
Unattended-Upgrade::Automatic-Reboot "false";
